.\" vyk(1) \(em man page for the vyakarana CLI
.\" Format: groff_man(7).  Render with `man -l docs/man/vyk.1`
.\"           or `groff -man -Tutf8 docs/man/vyk.1 | less -R`.
.\"
.\" Update procedure: this page mirrors `vyk --help` (src/main.cyr
.\" `print_help`).  When changing one, refresh the other by hand:
.\" nothing in scripts/smoke.sh or tests/vyakarana.tcyr reads this
.\" file, which is how the .TH line sat at 1.13.1 across the whole
.\" 2.x line.  Smoke probes `--help` output, never this page.
.\"
.TH VYK 1 "2026-10-20" "vyakarana 2.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vyk \- source-code tokenizer (vyakarana demo CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vyk
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fB\-\-\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR | \fB\-\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vyk
reads
.I FILE
(or standard input when
.I FILE
is
.BR \- )
and emits one NDJSON record per recognized token, or ANSI-coloured
source bytes when
.B \-\-theme=
is given.
.PP
Detection is automatic: extension first
.RI "(" .sh ", " .py ", " ".rs," " ...),"
then file name
.RI "(" Makefile ", " Dockerfile ,
and variants such as
.IR Dockerfile.dev ),
then a content sniff (shebang, BOM, magic bytes), and an asm
flavour vote for
.IR .s / .S .
Override with
.B \-\-language=<name>\fR.
.PP
Without
.IR FILE ,
.B vyk
prints help and exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-kinds
Print the ten token kinds and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
Print every loaded grammar name and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-language= name
Override extension/content detection. Run
.B \-\-list-languages
for valid names.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme= name
Render ANSI-coloured source instead of NDJSON. Bundled themes:
.BR default ", " dark ", " none .
See
.I docs/architecture/004-theme-palette-contract.md
for the kind\(->slot mapping.
.TP
.BI \-\-export-theme= format
Emit a theme file for the named editor format and exit. Formats:
.BR vscode " (theme.json),"
.BR helix " (theme.toml),"
.BR iterm " (.itermcolors plist)."
Pair with
.B \-\-theme=<name>
(before or after it) to pick the source palette (default:
.BR default ).
Takes no
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-handcoded
Route through the M1 hand-coded shell oracle. Regression
diagnostic for the shell grammar only; any other language is a
usage error.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options: every later argument is a
.IR FILE ,
even one starting with
.BR \- .
.TP
.B \-
As
.IR FILE :
read standard input (named
.I <stdin>
in messages). Detection can only use the content, so pass
.B \-\-language=
for input without a shebang or signature.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Tokenization produced one or more
.I error
token kinds (grammar gap or malformed input).
.TP
.B 2
Bad command-line usage: an unknown option, a missing or invalid
flag value (including a
.B \-\-language=
name no grammar has), too many arguments. Run
.B \-\-help
for syntax.
.TP
.B 3
I/O error: cannot read
.I FILE
(not found, not readable, or over the 1 MiB CLI cap), or cannot
write the output (a full disk, a closed or failing standard
output).
.TP
.B 4
No grammar matched
.IR FILE .
Run
.B \-\-list-languages
to see all bundled names, then retry with
.B \-\-language=<name>\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
NDJSON tokens to stdout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk script.sh\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
ANSI-coloured render with the dark theme:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-theme=dark file.rs\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tokenize standard input (detection needs a shebang or
.BR \-\-language= ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBgit show HEAD:app.py | vyk \-\-language=python \-\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tokenize an extensionless script via explicit language:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-language=python script\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit a VS Code theme file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-export-theme=vscode > theme.json\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Discover available grammar names:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-list-languages | grep ml\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
NDJSON records, one per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"kind":"keyword","start":0,"len":2}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where
.I kind
is one of:
.B ident, keyword, string, number, comment, operator,
.B punctuation, whitespace, preprocessor, error;
.I start
is a 0-indexed byte offset into
.IR FILE ;
and
.I len
is the token's byte length. Every input byte maps to exactly
one token's
.RI [ start ", " start + len )
span (the
.I coverage invariant\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I dist/vyakarana.cyr
Single-file bundle for downstream
.BR cyrius (1)
consumers. Includes all 46 grammars inlined as Cyrius string
literals.
.TP
.I grammars/<name>.cyml
Source grammar definitions. Authored by hand, embedded by
.B scripts/embed-grammars.sh
into the bundle.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cyrius (1),
.BR owl (1).
.PP
